<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch Q1 GDP seen up 3.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch Q1 GDP seen up 3.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economists polled by Reuters expect first-quarter Dutch gross domestic product (GDP) figures due on Thursday to show a year-on-year increase of 3.0 percent.</p>
<p>In the second, third and fourth quarters of 1996, Dutch GDP also showed a real year-on-year increase of three percent or slightly higher after a 1.6 percent rise in the first quarter.</p>
<p>Economists' forecasts for the first quarter of 1997 are</p>
<p>summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT---Date---Period---Indicator-----Consensus---Range------Pvs</p>
<p> 0730  29/5   Q1 97    GDP Yr/Yr     3.0 pct     2.7/3.4    3.0</p>
<p> 0730  29/5   Q1 97    GDP Qtr/Qtr   0.3 pct     0.0/0.7    0.5</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, Generale Bank, ING,</p>
<p>MeesPierson, J.P. Morgan, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Kelly, Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
